Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/7

**Problem.** In Daddy's Home, while the bed is not built, every search of the waxwood crates adds three more waxwood logs, so they can be farmed without limit (and sawn into planks). On OSRS you can't get duplicates of these quest logs (the OSRS Wiki's waxwood log page says so; nothing is copied from it).

**Change.** A crate search only tops the player up to the three the bed needs (`WAXWOOD_LOG_COUNT`), counting waxwood logs and waxwood planks in the inventory and the bank. With three already held, the crates give the existing "You search the crates but find nothing interesting." line, as they already do outside the stage.

**Tests.** New case in `DaddysHomeInteractionTest`: two searches leave three logs; with one plank held and one log banked, a search gives one log and the next gives nothing. `./gradlew :content:quest:test`. Checked in game on our build (desktop client): the first search gives the logs, the second says "You search the crates but find nothing interesting.".

**Caveats.** None known.

**Release note.** The Daddy's Home crates no longer hand out unlimited waxwood logs.

